# No personal data in tracked notes

Never write the operator's name, username, computer name, physical address, IP address, or email into a file git tracks. That includes `docs/`, `README.md`, commit messages, and any other path that is not gitignored.

Local-only notes under gitignored `.repo-kit/` follow the same ban.

Say "the operator", "this machine", or "the remote node". A public project hostname that is already part of the protocol docs may stay. `127.0.0.1` may stay.

```text
Bad:  the node at <ip> on <computer-name>
Good: a remote mainnet node answered GET /getinfo on port 16000
```
